1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Every AI tuning tool today is a chatbot guessing numbers. MetaECU Copilot is completely different.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:13,000
Pre-existing was our raw binary and catalogue; built entirely this week is our autonomous, verifiable calibration engine.

3
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,500
Built on Meta Muse and SAM 3.1, where physics and mechanical safety—not the model—have the final word.

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:24,000
We load the real stock flash from a Saab 9-3 1.9 TiD with a Bosch EDC16C39 ECU and GM F40 transmission.

5
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:30,000
The engine ingests 774 real Bosch maps, curves and constants with true addresses, axes and physical units.

6
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:36,000
The tuner simply specifies their goal in natural language or by voice: "Give me 450 Nm, maximum power".

7
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:43,000
Meta Muse Spark plans the calibration: torque curve, rail pressure ceiling, and smoke floor.

8
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:50,000
The 3D Map Explorer renders surfaces in real-time WebGL, inspecting friction and boost topology.

9
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:57,000
CRITICAL SAFETY INTERCEPT: The Deterministic Safety Gate computes friction at 90°C and rejects 450 Nm.

10
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:05,000
Peak effective torque of 438.5 Nm exceeds the 377 Nm GM F40 clutch limit. A human tuner might slip the clutch—MetaECU blocks it.

11
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:12,000
The violation report feeds back into the AI Self-Correction loop. Muse automatically replans inside the safe envelope.

12
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:18,000
Attempt two passes! 369 Nm effective torque, 1600 bar rail pressure, and zero torque spikes.

13
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:25,000
In the 3D Difference Matrix, we inspect the exact surgical delta applied to the calibration tables.

14
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:32,000
We run the Virtual Dyno Pull simulator: boost hits 1.45 bar, power reaches 185.4 HP, and 0-100 km/h drops by 1.6 seconds.

15
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:40,000
SAM 3.1 Vision Studio analyzes dyno charts, grounds torque valleys, and provides feedback on turbosystem response.

16
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:48,000
Real road telemetry from 33 WOT pulls proves turbo spool time dropped from 4.90s down to 1.34s.

17
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:55,000
The approved binary is exported with a verified Bosch 32-bit checksum (0xD01FE500), ready for physical flashing.

18
00:01:55,500 --> 00:02:04,000
Every tune ships with an Official Certificate of Safe Calibration, complete with cryptographic proof and safety seals.

19
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:14,000
Deployable serverless on Modal cloud, as a native zero-console desktop app, or headless CLI.

20
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:22,000
AI that proposes. Physics that disposes. MetaECU Copilot: Built for the Meta Global AI Developer Hackathon.
